    <GaugingStation location="Alness" name="Alness" number="4003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station in upland catchment. Flow affected by barrage constructed on Loch Morie.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Difficulties in current meter gauging at low flows. To date all flows contained. Adequately gauged to QMED. Rating derived from current meter gaugings to above QMED, simple extrapolation beyond AMAX1. Peak flow rating was revised in 2003 and a new single rating for high flows only, was judged to be suitable for whole period of record. Rating revised in 2016.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station; 20m wide fully contained river section with stable boulder control.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in April 2017 (WINFAP Files v5). Chart data between 1973 &amp; 1982 was digitised in 2016.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Sluices on Loch Morie, through which 45% of catchment drains, were constructed in 1979 for river regulation (to benefit fisheries). This influences mainly low flows through freshets.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mountainous headwaters, often snowy in winter. Bedrock predominantly Devonian sandstone with areas of Moinian metamorphics in the upper reaches of the catchment. Landuse mainly rough grazing and moorland with forestry. Minimal floodplains. Construction of barrage on Loch Morie in 1979.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SR</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to 50% of AMAX2 and AMAX3." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
